  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "Creation between glue lines depends only on the switching class",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Creation between glue lines depends only on the switching class (proved). For every cubic glue H, every two signings S and S' of H in one switching class, and every two lines a and b of H, removing a and gluing at b gives the same result in the plain edge-atom spaces X_S and X_S': both degenerate, or the same verdict for each far side. Proof: an edge atom's own lines force r0 = r1 = r2 = not p and leave its four inner points free enough (checked over all 256 assignments) that no knot used by PENDANT-LINE A's two-round rule contains an inner point; so creation between glue lines is creation in the signed glue (H, S), and switching only complements points, which changes no constrained set. Cross-checked: the glue block equals the signed glue's creation map on 22 placements (3,500 entries), and 136 random switchings of the 17 signed glues change no entry.",
  "dependencies": [
    "PENDANT-LINE-20261106-001A",
    "CHAIN-TRANSFER-20261106-001A",
    "SWITCH-READ-20261108-001A",
    "TRISUM-READ-20261107-001A",
    "TRISUM-READ-20261107-001B"
  ],
